        "topic": "Brake system principles",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2021",
        "question_text": "<p>In a hydraulic brake system, what principle explains why a small force applied at the brake pedal can generate a larger force at the wheel cylinders?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The hydraulic brake system operates on <b>Pascal's Law</b>, which states that pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished throughout the fluid. This allows a small force at the brake pedal to be multiplied at the wheel cylinders, generating sufficient force to apply the brakes.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
